ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57, D-94, D-118): layers laid over their parents directly when source-over
Library: resvg 0.50.0
Fixes: none (speed: tiny-skia draws a layer as a pattern through its high-precision pipeline)
Upstream: none yet: to be proposed to tiny-skia (a low-precision path for an untransformed pixmap) or resvg (ours)
Remove when: tiny-skia draws an untransformed source-over pixmap without its high-precision pipeline, or resvg composites layers so, or this patch no longer applies

render::render_group() lays a source-over layer neither turned, skewed nor reduced onto its parent with
its opacity directly (render::composite(): premultiplied, rounded to the nearest level), any other
through tiny-skia as before: draw_pixmap, which resvg used before 0.49.0, took half the time of a
document of large layers. The rounding differs from tiny-skia's by at most 3 levels. Requires the
three patches before it.

